    "0.1.4": {
        "info": {
            "author": "Amar",
            "author_email": "amar439412@gmail.com",
            "bugtrack_url": null,
            "classifiers": [
                "License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License",
                "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
                "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11"
            ],
            "description": "# Prompt Man\n\nPrompt engineering package for AI models.\n\n***Prompt Man*** introduces the concept of \"prompt-functions\", which is an alternative method for manual prompt engineering. \n\nIt's useful while making API calls to AI models, or any other development workflow that requires prompting.\n\nFor example, in a web app with a Flask/Django backend, you can use \n\nIt also makes prompt engineering more standardized. For example, if you are using GPT 3.5 to create a business report, then you can use the arguments to pass in the subject of the report and it then generates a templetized 100 page report.\n\nCurrent version includes prompt functions for the following AI model APIs:\n\n- ChatGPT - GPT 3.5, GPT 4 (OpenAI API)\n- Dall-E 2 (OpenAI API)\n- Stable Diffusion (Replicate)\n\nThe github repo also includes files that make api calls in the api folder. This demonsterates how a developer can use prompt-man to easily generate prompts and pass them directly as an object.\n",
            "description_content_type": "text/markdown",
